<!--
    Key bindings.

    Not listed in the .toc: the client loads Bindings.xml from an addon's
    folder by itself, and adding it to the .toc as well loads it twice.

    No double hyphen anywhere in this comment. XML forbids the pair
    inside a comment body, and every other file in this addon uses it as
    an em-dash, so the habit walks straight in here and the client
    answers with "not well-formed (invalid token)" and drops the whole
    file. That means the binding silently stops existing. Use a colon or
    a semicolon instead.

    The body runs in the global environment, which is why it calls a
    global rather than anything in our namespace: see
    YippYappHelper_Toggle in Core/Core.lua. Keeping the body to one call
    also means a binding cannot go stale against changes in here; the
    logic lives in Lua where it can be read and tested.

    BINDING_HEADER_YIPPYAPPHELPER and BINDING_NAME_YIPPYAPPHELPER_TOGGLE
    are set in Core/Core.lua and decide how this reads in the Key
    Bindings panel. Without the header the binding lands in an unnamed
    block at the bottom of the list.
-->
<Bindings>
    <Binding name="YIPPYAPPHELPER_TOGGLE" header="YIPPYAPPHELPER" runOnUp="false">
        YippYappHelper_Toggle()
    </Binding>
</Bindings>
